---
import asyncio

count = wire(0)
likes = wire(0)
liked = wire(False)
# Comprehension var is `k`, not `i`: leaked vars become page attributes and
# would collide with toggle()'s argument name in generated dispatch code.
items = wire([{"id": str(k), "name": "item-" + str(k), "done": False} for k in range(300)])

def increment():
    count.value += 1

async def slow_increment():
    await asyncio.sleep(0.5)
    count.value += 1

def toggle(i):
    items.value[i]["done"] = not items.value[i]["done"]

async def like():
    await asyncio.sleep(0.5)
    likes.value += 1
    # The server accepts every OTHER like. On a rejected one the predicted
    # `liked` class contradicts the server render and auto-reverts in the
    # browser — no error handling needed anywhere.
    liked.value = likes.value % 2 == 1
---
<div>
    <h1>Edge Stateless Mode</h1>
    <p>Every event below is one ~300&#8239;B msgpack <code>POST /_pywire/stateless</code>. No WebSocket.</p>

    <section id="counter">
        <h2>1 &middot; Optimistic counter</h2>
        <p>Count: {count}</p>
        <button id="inc" class="btn" @click.optimistic.optimistic-class-dim={increment()}>Increment</button>
    </section>

    <section id="slow">
        <h2>2 &middot; Slow action (500&#8239;ms) &mdash; spam-click it</h2>
        <p>The button dims instantly (predicted), stays dimmed ~500&#8239;ms while
        <code>await asyncio.sleep(0.5)</code> runs, then reconciles. Spam-clicking
        sends ONE POST total &mdash; the double-submit guard drops the rest.</p>
        <button id="slow-btn" class="btn" @click.optimistic.optimistic-class-dim={slow_increment()}>Slow increment</button>
    </section>

    <section id="list">
        <h2>3 &middot; Keyed list &mdash; 300 rows</h2>
        <p>Each row is its own keyed region (<code>key=item["id"]</code>). Toggling
        one row ships ONLY that row's HTML.</p>
        <ul id="rows">
        {$for idx, item in enumerate(items.value), key=item["id"]}
            <li class={'done' if item['done'] else ''}><span class="name">{item["name"]}</span> <button class={'tgl done' if item['done'] else 'tgl'} @click.optimistic.optimistic-class-done={toggle(idx)}>toggle</button></li>
        {/for}
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="likes">
        <h2>4 &middot; Wrong prediction (auto-revert)</h2>
        <p>The handler takes 500&#8202;ms and the server refuses every second like.
        Each click predicts <code>liked</code> instantly &mdash; on a refused click you
        can watch it hold for the round-trip, then snap back when the server's
        render disagrees.</p>
        <p>Server-accepted likes: {likes}</p>
        <button id="like" class={'liked' if liked else ''} @click.optimistic-class-liked={like()}>Like</button>
    </section>

    <p><a href="/about" id="link-about">About this demo</a></p>
</div>
